  "hints": [
    "The function must return an integer so callers can use the number.",
    "A semicolon turns an expression into a statement, discarding its value."
  ],
  "explanation": "In Rust, an expression without a semicolon evaluates to the block return value. Adding a semicolon to `result;` turns it into a statement that returns unit `()`. When the signature promises `i32`, returning `()` produces `E0308`. Rust has no `void` type."
